{"id": "EUVD-2026-86821", "enisaUuid": "f696fdb4-a0c5-33fc-8e5b-262eef221ab6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nhwmon: (corsair-cpro) Remove debugfs entries when probe fails\n\nccp_debugfs_init() registers debugfs files whose private data is the devm\nallocated ccp.  If hwmon_device_register_with_info() fails right after it,\nccp_probe() returns without removing them: the HID core then frees ccp,\nand ccp_remove() is not called for a failed probe, so the files stay\nbehind.  Reading one of them dereferences the freed pointer.\n\nRemove the debugfs entries on that error path.  debugfs_remove_recursive()\nwaits for readers already inside the show callbacks, so ccp is no longer\nreachable through debugfs by the time probe returns.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:11:33", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ae01aafd8214e48cb7eff11e92dfbf3778d52d9d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a5de53b08cc319dadce6fb68d33749ea37962952", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fdc1bc23ff59ee308042342cefcb918d6efba409", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4ee875c423c66c45d7ef7bbff403cd0e3971e0a2"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97967", "GHSA-w2f2-2vf7-7q6m"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0cbd63ed-b512-3ffd-bfa1-0f7c62bdb2ef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "0d6771ff-76c8-3d1f-9831-cd36e81854e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "0edf23c8-2b39-346e-bfb7-e76519909c9a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11"}, {"id": "14044955-b993-358a-b084-68688d8b5bf8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "1d5865fc-041f-344d-b1a9-f77904d84267", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "2b9c1a73-cc9d-3b83-b97b-8899d4189837", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5997eb60f896830126bc1783465b678b110e2fdd <4ee875c423c66c45d7ef7bbff403cd0e3971e0a2"}, {"id": "9e753247-e753-31c6-af5b-9e91390dc170", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5997eb60f896830126bc1783465b678b110e2fdd <a5de53b08cc319dadce6fb68d33749ea37962952"}, {"id": "d0345ad3-241f-3aa7-9da1-91fe4318c946", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5997eb60f896830126bc1783465b678b110e2fdd <fdc1bc23ff59ee308042342cefcb918d6efba409"}, {"id": "fd832d06-efce-31df-b484-81294d6f67f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5997eb60f896830126bc1783465b678b110e2fdd <ae01aafd8214e48cb7eff11e92dfbf3778d52d9d"}, {"id": "fdf27abf-0980-3b9b-845d-e182bca5bcfc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "38e7c76b-5d51-3dc7-80ff-5126c9d7b1b4", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}